<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Endurance Points</h1>
<p>Endurance is your stamina, shown in your <a cmd='#'>score</a> and your prompt. You 
spend it walking, more in rough land than on a road, and on hard work: 
climbing, swimming, many skills, shouting. When it runs low, you are too 
exhausted to go on, and must rest until it comes back.
</p><p>How much endurance you have depends on your constitution (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Constitution</a>) and your age: the young have the most, and it falls 
as you grow old (see <a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>).
</p><p>Endurance comes back by itself, but not while you fight. It comes back 
faster when you sit, faster still when you rest or sleep, and twice as fast 
in a sacred place, such as a temple. Hunger and thirst slow it down.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Constitution</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Rest</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>
</pre>




</div>